    story: Jerry Sandcaller was born into a village militia family, where weapons, footwork, and bruised pride were part of ordinary family life. As a child, Jerry Sandcaller lived through the noble stables, building strength and balance around animals, carts, mud, and long roads. As a young adult, Jerry Sandcaller worked through a deckhand work, trading comfort for balance, rope-burned hands, and distance from shore. They enter the dojo to choose the arena before the sea chooses for them.
